From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANYBOOK: vold: do not manage the disk the running system is
 on

On a PC booted from a USB stick (an OpenBook live stick), the stick
matches the usb disk source like any other USB drive. It holds no volume
vold can mount (its GPT has the system's own partitions), so vold gives
up ("disk:8,0 failed to identify") and SystemUI posts a "set up" notice
for it. The storage wizard behind that notice formats the disk, under the
running system.

Seen on the ROG Zephyrus G14 (OpenBook live, 2026-10-17 12:15Z): the
notification for disk:8,0, the stick itself, was tapped and opened
StorageWizardInit; nothing was formatted.

Skip a disk-add event when the disk holds the running system's own
partitions: the parent disk of /dev/block/by-name/userdata (else
by-name/super), read from /sys/dev/block/<maj:min>/../dev. Internal
storage on phones is never matched by a disk source, so nothing changes
there; a partition-less device (Cuttlefish's per-partition virtio disks)
has no parent "dev" file and is not matched.
---
 VolumeManager.cpp | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/VolumeManager.cpp b/VolumeManager.cpp
index 9846e12a..7b3a1992 100644
--- a/VolumeManager.cpp
+++ b/VolumeManager.cpp
@@ -106,6 +106,23 @@ static const unsigned int kSizeVirtualDisk = 536870912;
 
 static const unsigned int kMajorBlockMmc = 179;
 
+// The disk that holds the running system's own partitions ("userdata", else "super"), as "major:minor", or "".
+// On a phone that is internal storage, which no disk source matches anyway. On a PC booted from a USB stick (an
+// OpenBook live stick) it is the stick: it matches the USB source, holds no volume vold can mount, and SystemUI then
+// offers to set it up, which formats it under the running system.
+static std::string GetSystemDisk() {
+    for (const char* name : {"userdata", "super"}) {
+        struct stat st;
+        if (stat((std::string("/dev/block/by-name/") + name).c_str(), &st) != 0 || !S_ISBLK(st.st_mode)) continue;
+        std::string dev;
+        if (android::base::ReadFileToString(
+                    StringPrintf("/sys/dev/block/%u:%u/../dev", major(st.st_rdev), minor(st.st_rdev)), &dev)) {
+            return android::base::Trim(dev);
+        }
+    }
+    return "";
+}
+
 using ScanProcCallback = bool(*)(uid_t uid, pid_t pid, int nsFd, const char* name, void* params);
 
 VolumeManager* VolumeManager::sInstance = NULL;
@@ -217,6 +234,11 @@ void VolumeManager::handleBlockEvent(NetlinkEvent* evt) {
 
     switch (evt->getAction()) {
         case NetlinkEvent::Action::kAdd: {
+            if (GetSystemDisk() == StringPrintf("%d:%d", major, minor)) {
+                LOG(INFO) << "Not managing disk " << major << ":" << minor
+                          << ", which holds the running system's partitions";
+                break;
+            }
             for (const auto& source : mDiskSources) {
                 if (source->matches(eventPath)) {
                     // For now, assume that MMC and virtio-blk (the latter is
